# Backends that do NOT yet honour the display backing scale.
#
# Each one renders a 1x image that the compositor upscales, which is the blur
# users see on a HiDPI screen. Deleting a line is the proof the fix landed;
# the gate fails while a line is here but the backend is wired.
#
# The list is EMPTY: mac renders at `backing_scale` (2x on Retina), windows and
# web size their surfaces from the scale, and linux now binds `wl_output`, takes
# the largest scale among the outputs the surface has entered (plus
# `wl_surface.preferred_buffer_scale`), sets `set_buffer_scale`, sizes the EGL
# window in device pixels, and rasterises text at `fs * scale`.
#
# An entry belongs here only while a backend is genuinely unwired; the format is
# one backend name per line (`mac`, `windows`, `linux`, `web`).
